    confirmed: true,
    note: '((√5−1)/2)^(2^37); recomputed: 2.8847 × 10^−28,723,042,565. Heuristic only (\'probviously\' non-halting). arXiv:2509.12337 quotes an older, weaker figure (exponent 1,073,720,885, i.e. ~10^−224,394,395; the mantissa printed there, 4.84, does not reproduce; I get 9.05) and in Appendix C \'less than 10^−200 000 000\'. Content review 2026-10-14: the earlier display "less than 10^−28,723,042,565" was wrong, since 2.88 × 10^−28,723,042,565 is larger than 10^−28,723,042,565. Recomputed ((√5 − 1)/2)^(2^37) = 2.8847 × 10^−28,723,042,565 and ((√5 − 1)/2)^(2^37 + 1) = 1.7828 × 10^−28,723,042,565; the probability from a counter above 2^37 is below both, so "less than 3 × 10^−28,723,042,565" holds.'
